       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 4250 mg three times daily, which is 12,750 mg per day.\n- **Usual maximum:** about 2,550 mg per day (2,000 mg per day for extended-release). A single dose is typically 500\u20131,000 mg, and 850 mg is the largest standard immediate-release tablet.\n- **Risk:** This is about 5 times the daily maximum. It carries a serious risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney function.\n\nIt may be a typo. For example, you may have meant 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg per day) or 425 mg. Please check the intended dose, ideally with your resident or attending.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away. For example, I can enter metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals. Metformin is usually started low, such as 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, and then increased slowly."
